%N A398360 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^(k+1) * H(k) / (2*k+1)^2, where H(k) = A001008(k)/A002805(k) is the k-th harmonic number.
%H A398360 Ali Shadhar Olaikhan, <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/publication/373488370">An Introduction to the Harmonic Series and Logarithmic Integrals</a>, 2nd ed., 2023, section 4.5.6, pp. 334-335, eq. (4.130).
%H A398360 Michael I. Shamos, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20220206102634/https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.366.9997&amp;rep=rep1&amp;type=pdf">A catalog of the real numbers</a>, 2011. See p. 123.
%H A398360 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A398360 Equals 2*Im(Li_3(1+i)) - 3*Pi^3/32 - Pi*log(2)^2/8 + log(2)*G, where i is the imaginary unit, and G is Catalan's constant (A006752).
%F A398360 Equals -2*Im(Li_3((1+i)/2)) + Pi^3/64 + Pi*log(2)^2/16 + log(2)*G.
%e A398360 0.073553956728532169782441635371101315192562243821341...
%t A398360 RealDigits[2*Im[PolyLog[3, 1 + I]] - 3*Pi^3/32 - Pi*Log[2]^2/8 + Log[2]*Catalan, 10, 120, -1][[1]]
